W:2. For he came one night to her bed feet
W:And a grumbly guest I'm sure was he
W:Saying "Here am I thy bairn's father
W:Although I be not comely."
W:
W:3. And he had taken a purse of gold
W:And he had placed it upon her knee
W:Saying "Give to me my little young son
W:And take thee up thy nurse's fee.
W:
W:4. For I am a man upon the land
W:And I am a Silkie on the sea.
W:And when I'm far and far from land
W:My home it is in Sule Skerry.
W:
W:5. For it shall come to pass on a summer's day
W:When the sun shines bright on every stane
W:I'll come and fetch my little young son
W:And teach him how to swim the faem.
W:
W:6. And ye shall marry a gunner good
W:And a right fine gunner I'm sure he'll be.
W:And the very first shot that ever he shoots
W:Will kill both my young son and me."
